{
  "kanda": "aranya",
  "sarga": 10,
  "title": "Sri Rama's reply to Seetha",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/aranya/sarga10/aranyasans10.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/aranya/sarga10/aranyaitrans10.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Rama replies Seetha's enquiry as to why he should wage war to eliminate the demons. He says that it is only to protect the land from the atrocities of demons, and for safeguarding the decrepit sages under his scheme of protecting the helpless."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये अरण्य काण्डे दशमः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 10th chapter in Aranya Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "3.10.1",
      "label": "3.10.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "वाक्यम् एतत् तु वैदेह्या व्याहृतम् भर्तृ भक्त्या |\nश्रुत्वा धर्मे स्थितो रामः प्रत्युवाच जानकीम्",
      "iast": "vākyam etat tu vaidehyā vyāhṛtam bhartṛ bhaktyā |\nśrutvā dharme sthito rāmaḥ pratyuvāca jānakīm",
      "translation": "On hearing all of the words said by Vaidehi, in adoration of her husband, he who abides by virtue alone that Rama replied Janaki.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "bhartR^i bhaktyaa",
          "iast": "bhartṛ bhaktyā",
          "devanagari": "भर्तृ भक्त्या",
          "meaning": "husband, in adoration of",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vaidehyaa vyaahR^itam",
          "iast": "vaidehyā vyāhṛtam",
          "devanagari": "वैदेह्या व्याहृतं",
          "meaning": "by Vaidehi, said",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "etat vaakyam tu",
          "iast": "etat vākyam tu",
          "devanagari": "एतत् वाक्यं तु",
          "meaning": "all, words, but",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shrutvaa",
          "iast": "śrutvā",
          "devanagari": "श्रुत्वा",
          "meaning": "on hearing",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "dharme sthitaH raamaH",
          "iast": "dharme sthitaḥ rāmaḥ",
          "devanagari": "धर्मे स्थितः रामः",
          "meaning": "by virtue, abides, Rama",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "prati uvaaca jaanakiim",
          "iast": "prati uvāca jānakīm",
          "devanagari": "प्रति उवाच जानकीं",
          "meaning": "in turn, said [replied,] to Janaki.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.10.2",
      "label": "3.10.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "हितम् उक्तम् त्वया देवि स्निग्धया सदृशम् वचः |\nकुलम् व्यपदिशन्त्या च धर्मज्ञे जनक आत्मजे",
      "iast": "hitam uktam tvayā devi snigdhayā sadṛśam vacaḥ |\nkulam vyapadiśantyā ca dharmajñe janaka ātmaje",
      "translation": "\"You have said beneficial, friendlily words that are seemlier to your disposition, oh, lady, which are apt to speak of your familial brought up, for you are the daughter of virtue-knowing Janaka.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "devi",
          "iast": "devi",
          "devanagari": "देवि",
          "meaning": "oh, lady",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "dharmaj~ne janaka aatmaje",
          "iast": "dharmajñe janaka ātmaje",
          "devanagari": "धर्मज्ञे जनक आत्मजे",
          "meaning": "oh, virtue-knower, Janaka's, daughter",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kulam vyapadishantyaa ca",
          "iast": "kulam vyapadiśantyā ca",
          "devanagari": "कुलं व्यपदिशन्त्या च",
          "meaning": "familial [greatness,] that speak of",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "snigdhayaa tvayaa hitam sadR^isham vacaH uktam",
          "iast": "snigdhayā tvayā hitam sadṛśam vacaḥ uktam",
          "devanagari": "स्निग्धया त्वया हितं सदृशं वचः उक्तं",
          "meaning": "friendlily, by you, beneficial words, befitting to your [disposition]",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.10.3",
      "label": "3.10.3",
      "numbers": [
        3
      ],
      "devanagari": "किम् नु वक्ष्यामि अहम् देवि त्वया एव उक्तम् इदम् वचः |\nक्षत्रियैः धार्यते चापो न आर्त शब्दो भवेद् इति",
      "iast": "kim nu vakṣyāmi aham devi tvayā eva uk{}tam idam vacaḥ |\nkṣatriyaiḥ dhāryate cāpo na ārta śabdo bhaved iti",
      "translation": "\"What more shall I say, oh, lady, since it is said that 'a warrior handles a bow so that misery's tears cease to flow...' and this saying is iterated even by you...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "devi",
          "iast": "devi",
          "devanagari": "देवि",
          "meaning": "o, lady",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "aham kim nu vakSyaami",
          "iast": "aham kim nu vakṣyāmi",
          "devanagari": "अहं किं नु वक्ष्यामि",
          "meaning": "I, what [more,] verily, can I say",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "aarta shabdaH na bhavet iti",
          "iast": "ārta śabdaḥ na bhavet iti",
          "devanagari": "आर्त शब्दः न भवेत् इति",
          "meaning": "wailer's, yowl, shall not, be there, thus [misery's tears shall cease to flow -- Griffit]",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 13
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kSatriyaiH dhaaryate caapaH",
          "iast": "kṣatriyaiḥ dhāryate cāpaḥ",
          "devanagari": "क्षत्रियैः धार्यते चापः",
          "meaning": "Kshatriya-s, handle, bow",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "idam vacaH tvayaa eva uktam",
          "iast": "idam vacaḥ tvayā eva uktam",
          "devanagari": "इदं वचः त्वया एव उक्तं",
          "meaning": "this, word, by you, alone [perhaps,] said [iterated.]",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.10.4",
      "label": "3.10.4",
      "numbers": [
        4
      ],
      "devanagari": "ते च आर्ता दण्डकारण्ये मुनयः संशित व्रताः |\nमाम् सीते स्वयम् आगम्य शरण्याः शरणम् गताः",
      "iast": "te ca ārtā daṇḍakāraṇye munayaḥ saṃśita vratāḥ |\nmām sīte svayam āgamya śaraṇyāḥ śaraṇam gatāḥ",
      "translation": "\"Oh! Seetha, those shleterable sages of Dandaka forest have approached me sombrely on their own, and thus they came into my refuge...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "siite",
          "iast": "sīte",
          "devanagari": "सीते",
          "meaning": "oh! Seetha",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "samshita vrataaH",
          "iast": "samśita vratāḥ",
          "devanagari": "सम्शित व्रताः",
          "meaning": "sages, resolute, in practises",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sharaNyaaH daNDakaaraNye te munayaH",
          "iast": "śaraṇyāḥ daṇḍakāraṇye te munayaḥ",
          "devanagari": "शरण्याः दण्डकारण्ये ते मुनयः",
          "meaning": "those that are shelteable, in Dansaka forest, those sages",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "aartaa svayam aagamya",
          "iast": "ārtā svayam āgamya",
          "devanagari": "आर्ता स्वयं आगम्य",
          "meaning": "sombrely, on approaching",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "maam sharaNam gataaH",
          "iast": "mām śaraṇam gatāḥ",
          "devanagari": "मां शरणं गताः",
          "meaning": "my, refuge, they have gone in [came into.]",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.10.5",
      "label": "3.10.5",
      "numbers": [
        5
      ],
      "devanagari": "वसन्तः काल कालेषु वने मूल फल अशनाः |\nन लभन्ते सुखम् भीरु राक्षसैः क्रूर कर्मभिः",
      "iast": "vasantaḥ kāla kāleṣu vane mūla phala aśanāḥ |\nna labhante sukham bhīru rākṣasaiḥ krūra karmabhiḥ",
      "translation": "\"Subsisting on fruits and tubers, living at all the time in forests those sages are not getting quietude, as they are scared by the demons with invidious deeds...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "muula phala ashanaaH",
          "iast": "mūla phala aśanāḥ",
          "devanagari": "मूल फल अशनाः",
          "meaning": "tubers, fruits, eaters of",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vasantaH kaala kaaleSu vane",
          "iast": "vasantaḥ kāla kāleṣu vane",
          "devanagari": "वसन्तः काल कालेषु वने",
          "meaning": "living, time, after times [in all times,] in forest",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kruura karmabhiH raakSasaiH bhiiru",
          "iast": "krūra karmabhiḥ rākṣasaiḥ bhīru",
          "devanagari": "क्रूर कर्मभिः राक्षसैः भीरु",
          "meaning": "with invidious, deeds, by demons, scared",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sukham na labhante",
          "iast": "sukham na labhante",
          "devanagari": "सुखं न लभन्ते",
          "meaning": "quietude, not getting.",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.10.6",
      "label": "3.10.6, 7a",
      "numbers": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "devanagari": "भक्ष्यन्ते राक्षसैः भीमैः नर मांसोपजीविभिः |\nते भक्ष्यमाणा मुनयो दण्डकारण्य वासिनः\nअस्मान् अभ्यवपद्य इति माम् ऊचुर् द्विज सत्तमाः |",
      "iast": "bhakṣyante rākṣasaiḥ bhīmaiḥ nara māṃsopajīvibhiḥ |\nte bhakṣyamāṇā munayo daṇḍakāraṇya vāsinaḥ\nasmān abhyavapadya iti mām ūcur dvija sattamāḥ |",
      "translation": "\"The sages dwelling in Dandaka forest are being eaten away by fiendish demons that subsist on human flesh, and while being eaten away like that those eminent Brahmans have said to me, \"please come to our rescue...\"",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "munayaH daNDakaaraNya vaasinaH",
          "iast": "munayaḥ daṇḍakāraṇya vāsinaḥ",
          "devanagari": "मुनयः दण्डकारण्य वासिनः",
          "meaning": "sages, in Dandaka forest, dwellers",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "bhiimaiH nara maaMsopajiivibhiH",
          "iast": "bhīmaiḥ nara māṃsopajīvibhiḥ",
          "devanagari": "भीमैः नर मांसोपजीविभिः",
          "meaning": "fiendish, on human, felsh, that subsist",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "raakSasaiH bhakSyante",
          "iast": "rākṣasaiḥ bhakṣyante",
          "devanagari": "राक्षसैः भक्ष्यन्ते",
          "meaning": "by demons, are being eaten",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "te bhakSyamaaNaa",
          "iast": "te bhakṣyamāṇā",
          "devanagari": "ते भक्ष्यमाणा",
          "meaning": "they, while being eaten",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "dvija sattamaaH",
          "iast": "dvija sattamāḥ",
          "devanagari": "द्विज सत्तमाः",
          "meaning": "Brahmans, the eminet ones",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 15
        },
        {
          "itrans": "asmaan abhyavapadya",
          "iast": "asmān abhyavapadya",
          "devanagari": "अस्मान् अभ्यवपद्य",
          "meaning": "us, [to take possession of us] come to rescue",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "iti",
          "iast": "iti",
          "devanagari": "इति",
          "meaning": "thus as",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": 12
        },
        {
          "itrans": "maam uucur",
          "iast": "mām ūcur",
          "devanagari": "मां ऊचुर्",
          "meaning": "to me, said.",
          "anvayaIndex": 7,
          "verseIndex": 13
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.10.7b",
      "label": "3.10.7b, 8, 9a",
      "numbers": [
        7,
        8,
        9
      ],
      "devanagari": "मया तु वचनम् श्रुत्वा तेषाम् एवम् मुखात् च्युतम्\nकृत्वा वचन शुश्रुषाम् वाक्यम् एतत् उदाहृतम् |\nप्रसीदन्तु भवन्तो मे ह्रीः एषा तु मम अतुला\nयद् ईदृशैः अहम् विप्रैः उपस्थेयैः उपस्थितः |",
      "iast": "mayā tu vacanam śrutvā teṣām evam mukhāt cyutam\nkṛtvā vacana śuśruṣām vākyam etat udāhṛtam |\nprasīdantu bhavanto me hrīḥ eṣā tu mama atulā\nyad īdṛśaiḥ aham vipraiḥ upastheyaiḥ upasthitaḥ |",
      "translation": "\"This way when I have heard the words voiced by them, I comforted them verbally and avouched this way, \"Be gracious to me... you all... by which reason I am being addressed this way by this kind of eminent Brahmans, whom I should have actually addressed my self, this indeed is a dishonour for me...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "evam teSaam mukhaat cyutam vacanam shrutvaa",
          "iast": "evam teṣām mukhāt cyutam vacanam śrutvā",
          "devanagari": "एवं तेषां मुखात् च्युतं वचनं श्रुत्वा",
          "meaning": "this way, from their, mouth, fel, words, on hearing",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mayaa tu",
          "iast": "mayā tu",
          "devanagari": "मया तु",
          "meaning": "by me, but",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kR^itvaa vacana shushruSaam",
          "iast": "kṛtvā vacana śuśruṣām",
          "devanagari": "कृत्वा वचन शुश्रुषां",
          "meaning": "on making, vocal, vassalage - comforting them verbally",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vaakyam etat udaahR^itam",
          "iast": "vākyam etat udāhṛtam",
          "devanagari": "वाक्यं एतत् उदाहृतं",
          "meaning": "sentence, this one, avouched",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "prasiidantu me bhavantaH",
          "iast": "prasīdantu me bhavantaḥ",
          "devanagari": "प्रसीदन्तु मे भवन्तः",
          "meaning": "be gracious, to me, you all",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 14
        },
        {
          "itrans": "aham yat",
          "iast": "aham yat",
          "devanagari": "अहं यत्",
          "meaning": "I am, by which [reason]",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "upastheyaiH iidR^ishaiH vipraiH",
          "iast": "upastheyaiḥ īdṛśaiḥ vipraiḥ",
          "devanagari": "उपस्थेयैः ईदृशैः विप्रैः",
          "meaning": "those that are to be served, this kind of, [eminent] Brahamnas",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": 23
        },
        {
          "itrans": "upasthitaH",
          "iast": "upasthitaḥ",
          "devanagari": "उपस्थितः",
          "meaning": "they came to my fore",
          "anvayaIndex": 7,
          "verseIndex": 27
        },
        {
          "itrans": "eSaa mama atulaa hriiH hi",
          "iast": "eṣā mama atulā hrīḥ hi",
          "devanagari": "एषा मम अतुला ह्रीः हि",
          "meaning": "this, for me, immense, shame/dishonour, indeed.",
          "anvayaIndex": 8,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.10.9b",
      "label": "3.10.9b, 10a",
      "numbers": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "devanagari": "किम् करोमि इति च मया व्याहृतम् द्विज संनिधौ\nसर्वैः एव समागम्य वाक् इयम् समुदाहृता |",
      "iast": "kim karomi iti ca mayā vyāhṛtam dvija saṃnidhau\nsarvaiḥ eva samāgamya vāk iyam samudāhṛtā |",
      "translation": "\"Then I said before the Brahmans, \"what shall I do?\" All of them thus thronged and spoke this word.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "kim karomi iti ca",
          "iast": "kim karomi iti ca",
          "devanagari": "किं करोमि इति च",
          "meaning": "what, I shall do, thus, also",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mayaa vyaahR^itam dvija sannidhau",
          "iast": "mayā vyāhṛtam dvija sannidhau",
          "devanagari": "मया व्याहृतं द्विज सन्निधौ",
          "meaning": "by me, said, in Brahmins', in front of",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sarvaiH eva samaagamya",
          "iast": "sarvaiḥ eva samāgamya",
          "devanagari": "सर्वैः एव समागम्य",
          "meaning": "all, thus, thronging",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vaak iyam sam udaahR^itaa",
          "iast": "vāk iyam sam udāhṛtā",
          "devanagari": "वाक् इयं सं उदाहृता",
          "meaning": "word, this, spoke out.",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 11
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.10.10b",
      "label": "3.10.10b, 11a",
      "numbers": [
        10,
        11
      ],
      "devanagari": "राक्षसैः दण्डकारण्ये बहुभिः काम रूपिभिः\nअर्दिताः स्म भृशम् राम भवान् नः तत्र रक्षतु |",
